    "description": "Etobicoke General Hospital Phase 1 Patient Tower is a healthcare public-private partnership project in Ontario. The asset serves the William Osler Health System and the surrounding community through availability-based hospital infrastructure rather than commercial user-pay revenue. Its model is asset-heavy and contract-based because value depends on the construction, financing, and long-term delivery of a major clinical facility. Public project materials describe a new four-storey tower adding about 250,000 square feet to the hospital and housing critical emergency, intensive care, neonatal, and ambulatory services. Financial-close materials in 2016 identified DIF Infrastructure IV and Axium Infrastructure Canada II as equity sponsors, while public sources reviewed do not disclose their exact ownership percentages.",
